Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:14:07 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - player collision team on the global tick and
 region conversation input

collisions.enable-player-collisions=false: the hidden collideRule team is joined, left and removed through dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.guards.PlayerCollisionTeam, which posts the scoreboard change to the global tick (the base disabled the block because scoreboards are global-tick state; Paper also looked the team up with the wrong key on quit and shutdown). Bukkit Conversation input is delivered on the player's own region through dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.guards.ConversationInput instead of throwing inside the async chat chain.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java b/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java
index 8c2005bba5366abc7c475418f285015ec68f1854..d0c57a42d8efc73d67033002433de8e8e2e9f93a 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java
@@ -2760,9 +2760,8 @@ public class ServerGamePacketListenerImpl
         if (rawMessage.isEmpty()) {
             LOGGER.warn("{} tried to send an empty message", this.player.getScoreboardName());
         } else if (this.getCraftPlayer().isConversing()) {
-            if (true) throw new UnsupportedOperationException("Unsupported in region threading"); // Folia - region threading
-            final String conversationInput = rawMessage;
-            this.server.processQueue.add(() -> ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.this.getCraftPlayer().acceptConversationInput(conversationInput));
+            // Folia - region threading - the main-thread queue does not exist; SourbyCraft - deliver on the player's own region
+            dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.guards.ConversationInput.deliver(this.player, rawMessage); // SourbyCraft - owned conversation input
         } else if (this.player.getChatVisibility() == ChatVisiblity.SYSTEM) { // Re-add "Command Only" flag check
             this.send(new ClientboundSystemChatPacket(Component.translatable("chat.cannotSend").withStyle(ChatFormatting.RED), false));
         } else {
